    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ed25198_59942e3a",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 95,
      "author": {
        "id": 1302633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-10T17:52:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Quite a lot of registers are shared with multiple sensors and multiple configs.\n\nIf we blindly write to the registers, we might overwrite some other configuration and we may observe some unintended consequences. This helper function ensures that we are touching only those that we care about and leaving other configuration undisturbed.",
      "parentUuid": "a281f67a_415dfb5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "b072e1b9cd494dc458cb84e23a87e7469326ae04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b6dfe6e_8f84f9d5",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-04T20:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do we need to sleep here? also the comment says 500ms",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "b072e1b9cd494dc458cb84e23a87e7469326ae04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c68dc37_4052bb9c",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1302633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-10T17:52:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will fix the comment. Initially I added 500 ms and tuned it to 50 ms.\n\nRegarding the reason for the delay, it is a long story.\nData from external sensor can be handled using two types of triggers. One - every time the accelerometer data is ready, accel/gyro module can read external sensor data. The other approach is the external sensors themselves will trigger an interrupt when their data is ready. For the second approach, the external sensors data ready line has to be connected to the INT2 line of the accel/gyro module. In our case it is not connected. So we have to use accelerometer data ready as a trigger to read the external sensors.\n\nNow to use the I2C Pass through mode so that we can access external sensor register directly/quickly, we have to ensure that the sensor hub is not accessing the external sensors as part of the trigger(especially since I2C bus being slow). Hence we fake changed the external trigger and wait for some time to ensure that accel/gyro module is not reading external sensor data. This is the reason for the delay. The minimum recommendation is 5 ms as per one of the programming manual I read.\n\nI can tune this number further and see if there is any issue.",
      "parentUuid": "3b6dfe6e_8f84f9d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "b072e1b9cd494dc458cb84e23a87e7469326ae04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3aaaeefb_3f2e369c",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-04T20:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do we use a cache here instead of reading and writing?  (I am not against it, just want to understand)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 120,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "b072e1b9cd494dc458cb84e23a87e7469326ae04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66cc2b8e_8e21eb38",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1302633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-10T17:52:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So in this case, if the I2C master in accel/gyro is used as a pass-through, then it cannot be in master mode.\n\nBut if it were previously in master mode, then we have to ensure that it is switched back to that state after coming out of pass through mode. Pass through mode is primarily used to configure the registers in external sensors directly by EC. This will help expedite the configuration. Else EC has to write a lot of configuration to accel/gyro module which in turn will write to external sensors.",
      "parentUuid": "3aaaeefb_3f2e369c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 120,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "b072e1b9cd494dc458cb84e23a87e7469326ae04",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
