    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9da364d8_0d3d9bb1",
        "filename": "driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1302633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-10T17:52:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me present a hypothetical scenario.\n\nMagnetometer that we are trying to add can be either in cascade mode with accel/gyro module or can be directly connected through SPI/I2C. This entire sensor hub module comes into picture only when in cascade mode.\n\nWhen magnetometer is directly connected, then the magnetometer code will still refer to the function but will not use it. With this arrangement, we can simply disable/not define the Sensor hub without re-writing the magnetometer driver(except for adding support to direct connection). That way the compilation will work fine, stubbed out functions will be used and we dont need to build the sensor hub driver in direct mode(saving some code space).",
      "parentUuid": "edc76e48_d5ef4e7a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 31
      },
